#: includes/Admin/SettingsPage.php:286
msgid "AGT Sync for WooCommerce"
msgstr ""

#. Plugin URI of the plugin
#: agt-sync-for-woocommerce.php
msgid "https://github.com/shadow-software/agt-for-woocommerce"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: agt-sync-for-woocommerce.php
msgid "Publish your WooCommerce products as listings on American Gun Trader, and keep them in step. When a gun sells on AGT, the WooCommerce product is set out of stock automatically — so you never sell the same firearm twice. Free and open source; requires an American Gun Trader dealer account."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: agt-sync-for-woocommerce.php
msgid "Shadow Software LLC"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: agt-sync-for-woocommerce.php
msgid "https://shadowsoftware.com/"
msgstr ""

#: agt-sync-for-woocommerce.php:181
msgid "AGT Sync for WooCommerce requires WooCommerce to be installed and active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:36
msgid "What this plugin does"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:37
msgid "It publishes your WooCommerce products as listings on American Gun Trader, and keeps the two in step. The point of it is this: when a gun sells on American Gun Trader, the matching WooCommerce product is set out of stock automatically — so you cannot sell the same firearm twice, to two people, on two sites."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:39
msgid "What you need"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:41
msgid "A free American Gun Trader account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:42
msgid "An approved FFL on that account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:43
msgid "A complete dealer profile on that account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:44
msgid "A complete address on that account, with a city chosen from the dropdown — listings take their location from your account, not from the product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:47
msgid "How to connect"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:49
msgid "Click \"Connect to American Gun Trader\" on the Settings tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:50
msgid "You are taken to americanguntrader.com and asked to log in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:51
msgid "American Gun Trader shows you which store is asking, and what it will be able to do. You approve it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:52
msgid "You land back here, connected. There is nothing to copy and paste, and your store never sees your American Gun Trader password."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:55
msgid "How to set it up"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:57
msgid "Choose a default condition. Nothing publishes until you do — listing a used firearm as new is not something this plugin will guess at."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:58
msgid "Map your WooCommerce categories to American Gun Trader categories. A product will not publish until its category is mapped. Mapping a parent category covers everything beneath it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:59
msgid "Turn syncing on, and optionally click \"Sync all products\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:62
msgid "What happens afterwards"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:67
msgid "You edit a product"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:68
msgid "The listing is updated. Approved dealers publish with no review queue, so a price change stays live rather than pulling the listing down."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:71
msgid "A gun sells on American Gun Trader"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:72
msgid "The WooCommerce product is set out of stock, and a note is added to it saying why. This is the whole point of the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:75
msgid "A gun sells in your store"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:76
msgid "Its American Gun Trader listing is removed, so it is not offered to two buyers. Restocking the product brings the listing back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:79
msgid "You trash a product"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:80
msgid "Its listing is removed from American Gun Trader. Restoring the product from the trash brings the listing back — removal is reversible on both sides. You can switch this off in the settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:83
msgid "A product will not publish"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:84
msgid "The AGT Sync box on that product tells you exactly why — a description under 80 characters, no photo, an unmapped category, or a firearm with no manufacturer or caliber."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:87
msgid "You disconnect"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:88
msgid "Syncing stops. Your listings stay on American Gun Trader until you remove them there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:102
msgid "What is sent, and what is not"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:103
msgid "Only the product information needed to build the listing: its title, description, price, condition, weight, category, manufacturer, caliber and photos — plus your site address, once, at connection time, so you can recognise and revoke this store later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:104
msgid "No customer data, no order data, and no payment data ever leaves your store."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:104
msgid "The plugin does not read your orders or your customers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:106
msgid "Not supported yet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:107
msgid "Variable products. One variable product would be several American Gun Trader listings — one per caliber, say — and guessing which to publish would put a price in front of a buyer that does not apply to what they picked. Variable products are skipped and flagged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:109
msgid "Reviewing this plugin?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HowToPage.php:110
msgid "The connect flow needs a real American Gun Trader dealer account with an approved FFL, so it cannot be exercised without one. We will happily provide a sandbox dealer account — email support@shadowsoftware.com and we will set one up."
msgstr ""

